<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The night twin of `values/colors.xml`, and the reason the cold start does not flash.

    Resource qualifiers are resolved from the device's `uiMode` configuration, not from the
    theme's parent — so these values are picked up whenever the system is in dark mode, without
    `Theme.WishKaro` having to be a DayNight theme. That matters because the window background
    is applied before `onCreate`, long before `isSystemInDarkTheme()` has been read by anything.

    Each value is its `WishKaroPalette.DARK` twin.

    `ic_launcher_background` is deliberately NOT overridden here. A launcher icon is drawn by
    the launcher, which may be themed differently from the app, and an icon whose background
    changes under the user is an icon they stop recognising on the home screen. Android 13+
    themed icons are handled properly, by the `<monochrome>` layer, rather than by swapping the
    background out from under the normal one.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="wk_ground">#15131C</color>
    <color name="wk_accent">#E09A52</color>
    <color name="wk_ink">#F0EBE3</color>
</resources>
